.env
*.env
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
build/
.gradle/
*.class
.DS_Store
logs/
# runs/experiments.jsonl (the research trial log) stays gitignored -- it is
# a large, purely local research artifact (see research/experiment_log.py's
# DEFAULT_RUNS_PATH docstring). runs/live_signals.jsonl is the opposite: a
# low-volume, once-daily operational audit trail for the daily-tsmom-ensemble
# paper-trading signal runner (python/live/generate_daily_signal.py) that is
# deliberately git-committed, same treatment as any other operational log --
# see .planning/paper-trading-b-signal-runner.md. `runs/*` (not `runs/`)
# is required for the negation below to take effect -- git does not descend
# into a directory excluded via a bare trailing-slash pattern.
runs/*
!runs/live_signals.jsonl
# runs/spent_windows.json is the same shape: a small COMMITTED artifact
# derived from the gitignored experiments log by research/spent_windows.py,
# so CI can check CLAUDE.md's "unspent window" claim against something
# real. Without it that check passes vacuously wherever the log is absent.
!runs/spent_windows.json
# runs/krx_futures_liquidity.json is committed for a different reason than
# either of the above: it is the ONLY copy. KIS drops an expired
# single-stock futures contract's entire series -- measured 2026-09-16,
# expiries 2026-01 and later answer and 2025-12 and earlier return nothing
# at all -- so the front-month history this universe was selected from
# stops being fetchable within months and takes the selection's
# reproducibility with it. ~1.9MB of raw bars rather than only the
# medians, because a different question needs the bars. See
# .planning/rd-r-futures-liquidity-universe.md §3.3.
!runs/krx_futures_liquidity.json
# runs/krx_dayone_universe.json is committed for a THIRD reason, and the
# distinction matters because the obvious one does not apply: the 2019-01
# bars it ranks on are stable and KIS serves them indefinitely, so unlike
# the futures file above this is not the only copy of decaying data. What
# cannot be reconstructed is the CANDIDATE POOL -- it is today's live
# universe plus today's delisted list, and the delisted list only grows,
# so a re-run in a year ranks a larger pool and may return a different
# thirty. A point-in-time selection whose inputs move is not reproducible
# by re-running it. ~450KB: the chosen thirty plus all 2,180 ranked
# candidates, the second so a later reader can check the ranking rather
# than trust it. See .planning/rd-x-the-day-one-universe.md §3.
!runs/krx_dayone_universe.json
python/data/var/
# ...and the same store wherever a wrong working directory puts it. On
# 2026-09-10 a `cd python && PYTHONPATH=.` invocation resolved
# DEFAULT_DB_PATH ("python/data/var/klines.sqlite3") relative to `python/`
# itself, creating `python/python/data/var/` -- which the anchored rule
# above does not match, so a 36K SQLite file reached main via a `git add
# -A`. Unanchored, so depth cannot defeat it again.
**/data/var/
# Locally-generated runtime data for the live paper-trading signal runner
# (python/live/generate_daily_signal.py) -- the signal file(s) it writes,
# mirroring python/data/var/'s existing gitignore treatment for the kline
# cache above.
var/live/
